{
  "_": "The release table (tools/release_status.py): every configuration a release ships, one row each, and what proves it. A row is Ready only when every source below passes on the release build and no release-blocking defect (tools/defects.py <config> --release) is open for any of its configurations. 'boards' are criteria boards (tools/criteria.py): every cell PASS, recorded on the release build. 'runs' are verifications that are not boards: the newest file matching 'glob' must match 'pass' and name the release build ('build' is a regex whose group 1 is the srcversion, or 'version' whose group 1 is the MeshXFS version). A board on hosts that build the module against their own kernel names its build by the cluster marker that run recorded ('build_from_marker'), since its srcversion differs from this tree's .ko by construction. Every row carries the platform it runs on (data/platforms.json key), so a defect confined to another platform does not block it; the rig's rows run on the rig's Ubuntu 24.04. After the rows, every platform data/platforms.json marks released gets a row of its own, judged by its steps in tests/evidence/full_verify_<version>.log (the last result of each must be rc=0) and by the defects that reach its 2-node configurations on that platform. One row per independently verified unit (a configuration's board, a kernel's run), so a unit that has passed shows Ready whatever the others are doing.",
